From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:40:13 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/28] feat: Switch thread placement and a sampling profiler

host/switch_threads.cpp wraps libnx's threadCreate (-Wl,--wrap) so every
thread is seen, and lets the runner place them: the emulation thread on
core 1, the VU thread on core 2, the render thread keeps core 0, and a port
can send the threads it creates next to a core of its choice
(ps2_switch_new_thread_core, used for Mesa's glthread worker).

host/switch_sampler.cpp is a profiler for a console without perf: with
PS2_SAMPLE=<seconds> a thread pauses every other thread about once a
millisecond (svcSetThreadActivity, svcGetThreadContext3), records PC, LR
and frame-pointer frames, and at exit prints the hottest stacks and each
thread's core to the log, for addr2line against ps2run.elf.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
